---
/* Component — PageFooter
 * The page's footer bar. daisyUI's own .footer grid is rented: each direct
 * child of the slot becomes its own section (non-script/style/template
 * grandchildren auto-stack via daisyUI's inner grid), laying sections out in a
 * row — typically brand/copyright, version, and a link nav using daisyUI's
 * .footer-title and .link/.link-hover as-is.
 *
 * The outer element keeps daisyUI's .footer class, and this component's own
 * rule overrides it: display/grid-auto-flow are redeclared explicitly (matching
 * daisyUI's own .footer/.footer-horizontal values) so, like PageHeader, the box
 * model here is fully self-contained rather than leaning on daisyUI's layered
 * rules — and no .footer-horizontal modifier is needed in markup.
 *
 * A full-width edge-to-edge band like PageHeader: as a direct child of Page
 * (outside PageBody's inline inset) it spans the whole window width on its own,
 * and the sunken fill bleeds edge to edge with it, while this rule's inline
 * padding insets the section content — without shrinking the element's own box
 * — so it caps at --bravoixr-page-max and lines up with the page column above.
 * Themes with the page via the semantic dark override. */
---

<footer class="footer">
  <slot />
</footer>

<style>
  .footer {
    display: grid;
    grid-auto-flow: column;
    align-items: start;
    gap: var(--bravoixr-spacing-10);
    padding-block: var(--bravoixr-spacing-5);
    padding-inline: max(var(--bravoixr-spacing-10), calc((100% - var(--bravoixr-page-max)) / 2));
    background: var(--bravoixr-color-surface-sunken);
  }
</style>
